{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/layoutvaluekey"]}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutValueKey\/Value"],"anchor":"Associated-Types","generated":true,"title":"Associated Types"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutValueKey\/defaultValue"],"anchor":"Type-Properties","generated":true,"title":"Type Properties"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LayoutValueKey","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you create a custom layout by defining a type that conforms to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout","type":"reference"},{"text":" protocol, you can also create custom layout values","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that you set on individual views, and that your container view can access","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to guide its layout behavior. Your custom values resemble","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the built-in layout values that you set with view modifiers","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"like ","type":"text"},{"code":"View\/layoutPriority(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"View\/zIndex(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", but have a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"purpose that you define.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To create a custom layout value, define a type that conforms to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LayoutValueKey"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol and implement the one required property that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returns the default value of the property. For example, you can create"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a property that defines an amount of flexibility for a view, defined as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an optional floating point number with a default value of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["private struct Flexibility: LayoutValueKey {","    static let defaultValue: CGFloat? = nil","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Swift compiler infers this particular key’s associated type as an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optional "},{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/CoreFoundation\/CGFloat"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from this definition."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Set-a-value-on-a-view","text":"Set a value on a view"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Set the value on a view by adding the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View\/layoutValue(key:value:)"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"view modifier to the view. To make your custom value easier to work","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with, you can do this in a convenience modifier in an extension of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/View","isActive":true},{"text":" protocol:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["extension View {","    func layoutFlexibility(_ value: CGFloat?) -> some View {","        layoutValue(key: Flexibility.self, value: value)","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use your modifier to set the value on any views that need a nondefault"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["BasicVStack {","    Text(\"One View\")","    Text(\"Another View\")","        .layoutFlexibility(3)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Any view that you don’t explicitly set a value for uses the default","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value, as with the first ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Text","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" view, above.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Retrieve-a-value-during-layout","text":"Retrieve a value during layout"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Access a custom layout value using the key as an index"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on subview’s proxy (an instance of "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutSubview"},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and use the value to make decisions about sizing, placement, or other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"layout operations. For example, you might read the flexibility value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in your layout view’s "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutSubview\/sizeThatFits(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"adjust your size calculations accordingly:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["extension BasicVStack {","    func sizeThatFits(","        proposal: ProposedViewSize,","        subviews: Subviews,","        cache: inout Void","    ) -> CGSize {","","        \/\/ Map the flexibility property of each subview into an array.","        let flexibilities = subviews.map { subview in","            subview[Flexibility.self]